Let us test the Knuth-Plass paragraph optimizer on a long paragraph.

This is a really long paragraph meant to push the line-breaker to its limits. The breaking
algorithm must compute reasonable break points so that the resulting text fits the line measure.

aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa
bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb
cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc

A second paragraph follows. The line-breaker should not merge them, regardless of stretch.

Another paragraph, hopefully shorter, so the DP solution is observable.

EOF
